Source: libpqxx-vh
Section: libdevel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Cooper Larson <cooper@valkyrianlabs.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), python3, zstd
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/valkyrianlabs/libpqxx
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: libpqxx-vh-dev
Architecture: amd64
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libpq5 (>= ${sdk:LibpqMin}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: libpqxx ${sdk:Upstream} static C++ PostgreSQL SDK (Vaulthalla build)
 Development-only package of the Vaulthalla libpqxx SDK ${sdk:Version} (profile
 ${sdk:Profile}): the precompiled static libpqxx.a, the matching official headers and
 generated configuration header, and pkg-config metadata named libpqxx-vh.
 .
 Everything installs below /usr/lib/<multiarch>/libpqxx-vh plus
 /usr/lib/<multiarch>/pkgconfig/libpqxx-vh.pc, so it coexists with Ubuntu's
 libpqxx-dev. There is no runtime package: programs link the archive statically and
 load only the system libpq (libpq.so.5) at run time.
 .
 The files are byte-identical to the SDK archive published on Nexus; manifest.json
 records the upstream source and build provenance.
